  "source": "rem Prime Triplets\nrem https://projecteuler.net/problem=196\nrem Sum S(n) over the rows N1 and N2 of\nrem a number triangle, where S(n) adds\nrem the primes of row n that belong to a\nrem prime triplet\n\nuse numbers\nuse sequences\nuse io\nuse cli\n\noption N1 integer = 5678027\noption N2 integer = 7208785\n\nrem Row r holds r numbers from\nrem r (r - 1) / 2 + 1. A prime with two\nrem prime neighbours among the 8 around\nrem it starts a triplet, and joins its\nrem neighbours to it. Only rows n - 2 to\nrem n + 2 matter: sieve that strip, then\nrem scan the centres in rows n - 1 to\nrem n + 1 and mark primes of row n.\nAnswer = 0\nfor N in array N1 N2\n  First = (N - 2) * (N - 3) // 2 + 1\n  Len = 5 * N\n  Pr = array shape Len fill 1\n  Root = (First + Len) isqrt\n  for P in primes to Root\n    Start = (First + P - 1) // P * P\n    Start = Start max (2 * P)\n    Pr (Start - First till Len by P) = 0\n  end\n  if First equal 1\n    Pr 0 = 0\n  end\n  Offs = array shape 5 fill 0\n  for K in 0 to 4\n    R = N - 2 + K\n    Top = R * (R - 1) // 2 + 1\n    Offs K = Top - First\n  end\n  Mk = array shape N fill 0\n  M0 = Offs 2\n  for R in N - 1 to N + 1\n    Rows = R - N + 2\n    for C in 0 to R - 1\n      At = Offs Rows + C\n      if Pr At equal 1\n        Near = 0\n        for Dr in -1 to 1\n          Row = R + Dr\n          Base = Offs (Rows + Dr)\n          for Dc in -1 to 1\n            Col = C + Dc\n            if Col at least 0\n              if Col less Row\n                Near += Pr (Base + Col)\n              end\n            end\n          end\n        end\n        if Near at least 3\n          for Dc in -1 to 1\n            Col = C + Dc\n            if Col at least 0\n              if Col less N\n                if Pr (M0 + Col) equal 1\n                  Mk Col = 1\n                end\n              end\n            end\n          end\n        end\n      end\n    end\n  end\n  Row0 = N * (N - 1) // 2 + 1\n  Hit = (Mk equal 1) indices\n  Answer += (Row0 + Hit) sum\nend\nAnswer print\n",
